Goal: Finalize the existing uncommitted triage work in this repository by completing its DATA ACQUISITION stage only (the evaluation pipeline is a later, separate task). Keep and build on the existing cubs_edge_lab/triage*.py modules and tests.

OWNER AUTHORIZATION (verbatim decision of the repository owner, 2026-10-09T07:10Z): "Yes, local-only as described": the project may make approximately 200 rate-limited MLB Stats API requests for league-wide season statistics, seasons 2017-2025, to build cohort tables that stay local; only aggregates and a few short attributed examples are published. This is the owner's reading of MLBAM's "individual, non-commercial, non-bulk use" terms for this personal, non-commercial research. Do perform these requests in this session (network access is available); do not commit any response content.

Requirements:
1. Fetch, through the existing client (sequential, at most 2 requests per second, cache and manifest), league-wide regular-season statistics for sportIds 1, 11, 12, 13, 14, groups hitting and pitching, seasons 2017 through 2025, paginating as needed. Never request season 2026. Record every request in research/raw_manifest.json; responses stay under ignored data/.
2. Build local cohort tables (ignored data/, e.g. data/cohorts/*.json) for cohorts 2018, 2019, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025: the pool (typeCode DFA, "elected free agency", Nov 1 to Dec 31 of Y, from the cached transactions), per-player season-Y and Y-1 statistics by level, highest level in Y, age on the election date, and MLB PA/IP in Y and Y-1. Join only on person IDs. Do NOT build outcome labels (season Y+1) for any cohort in this task.
3. Report coverage per cohort in research/DATA.md and research/data_summary.json (aggregates only): pool size, players matched to any season-Y statistics, unmatched count with reasons, and the share with no MLB appearance in Y.
4. Measure the Chicago Cubs (team id 112) offseason signings for 2021-22 through 2025-26 (Nov 1 to Mar 31): first list the observed (typeCode, typeDesc) groups among Cubs transactions, then count minor-league contracts and spring-training invitations with explicit, tested matching rules; record counts per offseason, the rules, unmatched cases, and at most 5 short examples per offseason in research/data_summary.json and research/DATA.md. Record the median of the yearly combined counts as `k_basis`.
5. Tests (offline, fixtures only, no tracked-file writes, all existing tests still pass): fetch pagination and the season ceiling (a fake client asserting no request has season 2026 or later), cohort selection and the as-of window, ID-only joins, coverage counting, and the Cubs matching rules.

Integrity: never invent or alter values; every number in DATA.md must come from the code's outputs; label FACT/INFERENCE/UNKNOWN. If the API cannot provide something, report it as UNKNOWN with the measured reason.
